The fault is isolated to the search→rate call path. I have enough to answer, so I'm stopping here.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, service_name, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.5)/1e6 p50_ms, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('search','rate','geo') GROUP BY 1,2,3 ORDER BY 1,2,3", "claim": "search's client span to rate.Rate/GetRates takes ~1538ms p50 while rate's server span stays ~0.6ms; search→geo stays ~0.5ms."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT c.duration/1e6 client_ms, s.duration/1e6 server_ms, epoch(s.time)-epoch(c.time) start_lag_s, (epoch(c.time)+c.duration/1e9)-(epoch(s.time)+s.duration/1e9) end_gap_s FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND c.span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND c.attr_span_kind='Client' AND s.service_name='rate' LIMIT 15", "claim": "Rate server span starts ~1.5s after search's client span starts but ends at the same moment; delay is before the server receives the request."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT floor(duration/1e8)/10 AS bucket_s, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1", "claim": "Search's outgoing rate calls cluster at 1.3–1.5s with a tail near 2.5–2.8s; no errors, status Unset."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.5)/1e6 p50_ms, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('search','frontend') AND (span_name LIKE '%Nearby%' OR span_name LIKE 'HTTP /hotels%') GROUP BY 1,2,3 ORDER BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Search's Nearby server spans rise to ~1538ms p50, and frontend's HTTP /hotels rises to ~1546ms p50 from ~3.8ms in normal period."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
